      "stop_reason": "agent_finished",
      "final_text": "All four tests now pass. I fixed four defects in `src/inventory/`:\n\n- **`Reservation.active` (`models.py`):** the comparison was inverted. It returned true once a reservation had expired, so active holds were never counted. It now returns `now < expires_at`.\n- **`reserve` (`store.py`):** it checked the request against total stock. It now checks against `available(sku)`, so existing active holds count.\n- **`release` (`store.py`):** it raised `KeyError` for an unknown or already-released id. It now ignores them, as the docstring says.\n- **`commit` (`store.py`):** the docstring says an unknown or expired reservation raises `KeyError` and leaves stock unchanged. The old code would have committed an expired one. I added an active check before the stock is touched. No test covers this case, so it is untested.",
